{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the vascular surgery team. You've been admitted tonight because of the ulcers on your left foot and the blockage we saw in your leg artery last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I remember. The angiogram showed a bad blockage in my left leg, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:17:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It's a near-occlusive lesion in the left superficial femoral artery. We’re planning to fix that with a procedure called an endarterectomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that like a bypass? I thought I was getting a bypass."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:19:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We initially planned a bypass using your own vein, but we need to check first if the vein is usable. That’s why we’re doing a vein mapping ultrasound tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:20:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. And what about my blood thinner? I’m on Coumadin for my mechanical valve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. We’re stopping your Coumadin for now and starting a heparin drip. That’s safer around surgery. We’ll restart Coumadin after the procedure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:22:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the heparin will be adjusted based on my blood tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll monitor your PTT and adjust the drip to keep it in the right range. Once your INR is back up to 3.0–3.5, we’ll stop the heparin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll need dialysis too—usually on Mondays, Wednesdays, Fridays."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2193-11-01 22:25:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve scheduled dialysis for tomorrow. The transplant nephrology team will be following you as well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your vein mapping ultrasound was done this morning. The greater saphenous vein in your left leg is patent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So we can use it for the bypass?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll find out during surgery. Sometimes that vein was used in prior heart surgery and might not be available."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a CABG years ago—could they have taken it then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. If it was harvested, we’ll have to use a different approach. But we have a backup plan—endarterectomy with patch angioplasty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2193-11-02 10:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, as long as the blood flow gets fixed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2193-11-02 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You just finished dialysis. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2193-11-02 12:31:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little tired, but okay. No cramps this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2193-11-02 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep monitoring your labs, especially potassium and fluid status."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2193-11-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning your surgery for tomorrow morning. Any questions before then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2193-11-03 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just—what exactly is an endarterectomy?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2193-11-03 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We open the artery and remove the plaque buildup. Then we sew in a patch to keep it open. It’s a direct way to fix the blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2193-11-03 08:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll be in the ICU after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2193-11-03 08:06:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the VICU for one night, just to monitor your heart and circulation closely, given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you're back from surgery. The procedure went well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did you use my vein for the bypass?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We explored the greater saphenous vein, but it was tied off—likely used in your prior CABG. So instead, we did a femoral endarterectomy with patch angioplasty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that as good as a bypass?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For your type of blockage, yes. It restores blood flow and should help your foot ulcers heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2193-11-04 14:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’m glad it’s done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2193-11-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.8. We’re still running the heparin drip but getting close to stopping it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2193-11-05 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When will I be back on Coumadin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2193-11-05 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re already on it—4 mg daily. Once your INR hits 3.0–3.5 and stays there, we’ll stop the heparin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2193-11-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—am I back on all of them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2193-11-05 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, including tacrolimus, sirolimus, and aspirin. The transplant team reviewed everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2193-11-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The podiatry team cultured your foot ulcer today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2193-11-05 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was there an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2193-11-05 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The culture grew coagulase-negative staph. It’s a common skin bacterium, but we’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2193-11-05 10:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need different antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2193-11-05 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. You’re already on IV vancomycin on dialysis days, which covers it. We’ll continue that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs show your INR is now 3.9."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that too high?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s slightly above our target of 3.0–3.5, but since we’re stopping the heparin today, it should stabilize."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. Can I start walking more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the physical therapist saw you today. You’re doing well. They recommend home physical therapy after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need help at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2193-11-06 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, home nursing and physical therapy. You’ll need help with wound checks and mobility at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re healing well. The incision looks clean, no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my foot ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Podiatry says it’s stable. Improved blood flow should help it heal over time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on a special diet too, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 2 grams sodium and 2 grams potassium. It’s important for your heart and kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2193-11-07 08:37:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep that up at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call us if you have fever over 100.5, increased pain, redness spreading from the incision, or drainage that’s yellow or green."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And activity?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can walk and go up and down stairs, but no heavy lifting—nothing over five pounds—for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I shower?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2193-11-08 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, let water run over the incision, pat dry. No soaking in a tub yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2193-11-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. We’ve arranged home nursing, physical therapy, and your follow-up with Dr. Patel in two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2193-11-09 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I keep taking Coumadin, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2193-11-09 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 4 mg daily. Continue all your other meds too—especially the transplant and dialysis ones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2193-11-09 10:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home today. The team is proud of your progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Remember: elevate your leg when sitting, eat small frequent meals, and keep up with your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And call if anything seems off."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:10:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your incision can stay uncovered unless there’s drainage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:13:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Just a dry dressing if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Rest well and keep building your strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2193-11-10 08:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2193-11-01 22:07:00",
    "admission_end": "2193-11-10 19:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with end-stage renal disease, a history of pancreas and kidney transplants, and a mechanical heart valve was readmitted for treatment of left foot ulcers and a significant blockage in the left superficial femoral artery. She underwent vein mapping, which showed a patent greater saphenous vein, but during surgery, it was found to be tied off, likely from a prior CABG. As a result, she had a left femoral endarterectomy with patch angioplasty instead of a bypass. She was managed postoperatively in the VICU, transitioned from heparin to Coumadin, and maintained on her home immunosuppressive and dialysis regimen. Cultures from her foot ulcer grew coagulase-negative staph, but no treatment change was needed. She worked with physical therapy, was deemed safe for discharge home with home health services, and was given detailed wound care and activity instructions. Her INR was therapeutic at discharge, and she was scheduled for follow-up in two weeks.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerosis of native arteries of the extremities with ulceration",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Complications of transplanted kidney",
      "Pancreas replaced by transplant",
      "Hypertensive chronic kidney disease, unspecified, with chronic kidney disease stage V or end stage renal disease",
      "Systolic heart failure, unspecified",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Ulcer of other part of foot",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of unspecified type of vessel, native or graft",
      "Aortocoronary bypass status",
      "Old myocardial infarction",
      "Heart valve replaced by other means",
      "Automatic implantable cardiac defibrillator in situ",
      "Long-term (current) use of anticoagulants",
      "Personal history of tobacco use",
      "Long-term (current) use of aspirin",
      "Surgical operation with transplant of whole organ causing abnormal patient reaction, or later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of operation",
      "Renal dialysis status"
    ]
  }
}
